  "caveats": [
    "Full-detail imported beech.obj slot0 is canopy-like geometry assigned bark material, not leaf material. Its slot1 uses the Standard trunk material.",
    "Bark near and middle slot1 alpha samples are 254 or 255, including one-pixel repeat margins. This supports opaque authored texels for scoped tests, not a shader-state change.",
    "Distant bark underside includes 517 zero-alpha texels and 1705 texels below 128. Its sides include 10 of 169254 texels below 128, increasing to 52 with one-pixel repeat margin. Alpha cannot be discarded globally.",
    "Stored Mode3, SrcBlend1, DstBlend10 and ZWrite0 do not establish the live shader alpha path. Small leaf materials have no valid keywords; ALPHAPREMULTIPLY_ON is stored only as an invalid keyword.",
    "Unhealthy sapling material 1406518094360602383 has cutoff .26 and color(1,.562221,.345588,1), compared with cutoff .5 and white for healthy and ordinary small leaves. It also has RippleDistance 1 rather than .5.",
    "Healthy and unhealthy sapling child transforms have uniform scale .45. Small-tree children are identity. Prefab root editor translations must not be treated as mesh-local placement.",
    "Large blob foliage samples a baked canopy image; small foliage samples a branch image. Similar UV extents do not make those source compositions interchangeable.",
    "Existing leaf normals describe original shapes and do not establish compatibility with replacement leaf artwork.",
    "Mesh rendering, mip filtering, compression, wind, weather, lighting, shader behavior and final acceptance require separate evidence."
  ],
